---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import ProjectDetail from '../../components/ProjectDetail.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const nav = {
  about: 'About',
  projects: 'Projects',
  experience: 'Experience',
  skills: 'Skills',
  contact: 'Contact',
  menu: 'Open navigation',
  navigation: 'Main navigation',
};

const facts = [
  { label: 'Effort', value: '≈ 250 hours' },
  { label: 'Dataset', value: '731 positive · ≈ 2,000 negative images' },
  { label: 'Model', value: 'YOLOv11-L · 640 × 640 · 160 epochs' },
  { label: 'Deployment', value: 'Laptop · NVIDIA Jetson platforms' },
];

const sections = [
  {
    title: 'Objective and ownership',
    paragraphs: [
      'The project explored early visual knife detection in live camera streams as a research prototype. I completed it independently and started with very little prior computer-vision experience, learning Python, data labeling, YOLO training and edge deployment as the project progressed.',
      'The result is a functional prototype for experimentation, not a certified or market-ready safety system.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Self-recorded dataset',
    paragraphs: [
      'All images were recorded specifically for the project, including frames extracted from my own videos. The final working dataset contains 731 images with knives and approximately 2,000 negative examples without a knife. I manually reviewed the labels and later used auto-labeling to accelerate the process; total labeling effort was approximately 40–60 hours.',
      'An 80/20 training-validation split and a separate small test set were used. Because frames from the same video scenes may have been randomly distributed between training and validation, benchmark metrics are not published yet. Before publishing them, the data should be re-split by scene or source video and evaluated again on an independent holdout set.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Training and iteration',
    paragraphs: [
      'The selected configuration used YOLOv11-L at 640 × 640 pixels for 160 epochs. Across approximately 20–50 training runs, I iterated on the dataset and training setup rather than treating the first output as final.',
      'Early versions recognized many hand-held objects as knives because the dataset did not contain enough representative negative scenes. Adding approximately 2,000 negative examples reduced these false detections substantially.',
    ],
    bullets: [
      'One labeled class: knife',
      'Self-recorded positive and negative scenes across different lighting and backgrounds',
      'Repeated review of weak bounding boxes and false-positive examples',
      'Final Precision, Recall and mAP pending a leakage-resistant re-evaluation',
    ],
    media: [
      {
        src: '/images/knife-detection-false-negative.png',
        alt: 'Live camera frame showing scissors correctly not classified as a knife',
        caption: 'Negative test example · the scissors were correctly not classified as a knife',
        variant: 'contain',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Live deployment',
    paragraphs: [
      'The model was executed from a live webcam on a Lenovo Yoga Slim 6 and on NVIDIA Jetson platforms, including an Orin Nano Super. The laptop produced an observed 6–10 FPS, but device-specific figures will only be presented as benchmarks after model, input resolution and measurement method have been standardized.',
      'The prototype was demonstrated in unfamiliar scenes and across different lighting conditions and backgrounds, but reliability drops with occlusion and unusual knife shapes.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Cost-aware training infrastructure',
    paragraphs: [
      'Repeated cloud GPU usage would have created a continuing operating expense, so I considered that approach against owning a reusable workstation. In March 2025, I sourced almost all components second-hand and built a local AI workstation for approximately €910. A provider-specific break-even calculation is not presented because the original cloud quotations and total training hours were not retained.',
    ],
    table: {
      headers: ['Decision factor', 'Local workstation'],
      rows: [
        ['Core hardware', 'NVIDIA Tesla T4 · Ryzen 7 5800X · 64 GB RAM · 1 TB Samsung 990 Pro'],
        ['Acquisition', 'Almost entirely second-hand, including a negotiated CPU/mainboard/RAM bundle'],
        ['Iteration', 'Available for repeated training without a new usage fee for each run'],
        ['Residual value', 'Second-hand listings suggest substantial residual value, but no resale price has been confirmed'],
        ['Energy use', 'Training intentionally scheduled during local PV generation after the 2 kWh battery was full; the exact solar share was not measured'],
      ],
    },
  },
  {
    title: 'Result and limitations',
    paragraphs: [
      'The project produced a working live demonstration and reusable training hardware. It also showed that data composition can matter more than simply increasing model size. The current model is an experimental prototype: it is not certified, not market-ready and should not be interpreted as a reliable public-safety product.',
      'A new uncut demonstration video, standardized device benchmarks and a grouped dataset split are the next evidence steps. Only then will Precision, Recall, mAP and comparable FPS values be published.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Live Knife Detection Prototype | Raphael Erwig"
  description="Case study: self-recorded data, YOLOv11-L training, false-positive analysis, edge deployment and cost-aware local AI infrastructure."
  canonicalPath="/projects/knife-detection/"
  enPath="/projects/knife-detection/"
  dePath="/de/projekte/messererkennung/"
>
  <Header
    lang="en"
    labels={nav}
    languageHrefs={{ en: '/projects/knife-detection/', de: '/de/projekte/messererkennung/' }}
  />
  <ProjectDetail
    backHref="/#projects"
    backLabel="Back to projects"
    eyebrow="AI · Computer Vision · Python"
    title="Live knife detection with a self-trained YOLOv11-L model"
    lead="An independent research prototype covering self-recorded data, approximately 20–50 training runs, false-positive analysis, edge deployment and the economics of local AI infrastructure."
    status="Functional research prototype · not a safety product"
    {facts}
    {sections}
    heroMedia={{
      src: '/images/knife-detection-positive.png',
      alt: 'Live camera frame showing one knife detected with an 82 percent displayed confidence score',
      caption: 'Current demonstration · one knife detected with 82% displayed confidence',
      variant: 'contain',
    }}
    nextLabel="Next case study"
    nextHref="/projects/high-speed-drone/"
    nextTitle="Performance-Oriented Drone Prototype"
  />
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
